The totals are summaries, not substitutes for named gates. EXPECTED-OUTCOMES records79 exact names/status/message values per phase. Seventy-one selected rows map by unique name to completed main baseline/column/block/both RUN receipts. Renamed column file IDs are explicitly recorded in CASE-TRANSFER. The retained main fixtures were larger; the landing cleanup is not claimed byte-identical, and the new run must validate exact new files. Grid baseline statuses/messages come from the sealed fixture-check discovery; isolated reproduction is still required. Grid-only/all-three PASS and no interaction changes are predictions, not prior runtime evidence.

The baseline first checks the four hidden Grid failures at after-parent-width; unexpected stages or isolated behavior stop and restore. Every phase requires all50 tracked controls PASS and exact unchanged control messages. Each full79-case map must then equal its named expected map. All raw outcomes, discrepancies and transitions are retained before an expectation failure. Calibration failures also stop and restore; failed predictions are evidence, not grounds to weaken assertions.

## Restoration / readiness

Preparation has been enabled after the main campaign reached terminal/restored/rebuild0 with empty recovery errors and matching BEFORE/FINAL. Preparation requires HEAD90e7, an empty index, exact baseline/guard/tracked-test bytes, absent old/current temporary tests, pinned support and metadata, and snapshots all24 original source files. The remaining five guarded sources must equal HEAD. Any newer HEAD needs a separately reviewed source-role transfer, not merely a changed command argument.

prepare.py is byte-identical to the disabled Grid controller. run_wpt.py is byte-identical to the reviewed boundary-v2 runner. The exception/restoration tail is unchanged: restore all24 independently, remove only owned installed tests, rebuild originals despite receipt-write failures, then verify full original source/HEAD/index/resources and test absences. Final restoration includes preserved unaccepted prototypes; phase builds exclude them. The restored source must not be confused with an accepted candidate installation.

